  "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=\\frac{{X}^{2}}{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $8$ | $2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $8$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in {0,2,8}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for both $Y=2$ and $Y=8.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0) & =0.25 \\\\ P(Y=2) & =0.1+0.1 \\\\ P(Y=8) & =0.4+0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.55$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=2,b=8,d=0.55,$ and $a+b+d=10.55.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
